  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_012 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.725 acc. The key finding is that multiprofile + transformer aggregation strongly outperforms singleprofile and avgpool. The fusion method (weighted vs. concat) has not yet been tested in the multiprofile + transformer setting. Question: Does concat fusion (which preserves full modality information before a learned projection) outperform weighted fusion (a fixed linear combination) when combined with transformer aggregation? This is a clean single-variable A/B test against config_012, changing only fusion from weighted to concat. Rationale: This is the most direct and informative next step—it exploits the proven architecture (multiprofile, transformer, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l) while resolving the one untested design axis. If concat wins, we get a new best; if not, we confirm weighted fusion is optimal and can pivot to RNA/image encoder variations. Expected cost is similar to config_012 (~3.6–3.8 GPU hours), since the architecture is identical except for the fusion head, making this a low-risk, high-information experiment."
